riley.mclaugh...@gmail.com wrote:
> I used a blessed scroll of enchant weapon on Magicbane and it went to
> +3. Is there a way to reduce its enchantment back to +2? Engraving
> doesn't dull it, cursed scrolls of enchant weapon have had no effect,
> Drain Life has failed.

Drain life/c?enchat weapon/disenchanter or cursing it and engraving
will work.

All of those are bad ideas--  +3 is better than +2, and Magicbane is
best at +7.  Some of the less important magical effects are less
likely at +7, but the damage more than offsets that and the most
important athame/artifact effects (1-turn E, magic resistance, curse
resistance) are unaffected by enchantment level.  Scaring/confusion/
probing/cancellation are affected; the first 2 are better (and more
reliably) achieved through the 1-turn E effect.  Probing is mildly
interesting and you get the more interesting parts for free if you
have a stethoscope--it's certainly not worth a damage reduction.
Cancellation is almost completely useless against most monsters, and
too unreliable to be worth much as a Magicbane effect against the
rest.

Some spoilers recommend +2 over +7, but they're simply wrong.



